Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Changes: silent language-code metadata, short bilingual passage scripts, and
separate full-history writer orchestration. The original TTS implementation
has not been copied wholesale.

The vocal direction examples in server/prompts.ts and the tag vocabulary in
shared/voice-tags.ts are adapted from MaestroTutor's VOICE_TAG_PERSONA_GUIDELINES,
copyright 2025 Roni Tervo, under Apache-2.0.

Pitch-preserving playback uses SoundTouchJS 2.1.1 packages, copyright Steve
'Cutter' Blades, under Mozilla Public License 2.0. Upstream source and notices:
https://github.com/cutterbl/SoundTouchJS
License: https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
The dependency sources are available through npm and the locked package versions.
The unmodified SoundTouchJS modules are bundled into the audio worklet.

The Lyria quality-mode configuration and speech-keyed music compression are
informed by Roni Tervo's DrawnExplainers (lib/music.mjs and lib/build.mjs) and
MaestroTutor. This implementation generates a continuous live stream and uses
causal playback mixing instead of the offline FFmpeg loudness-normalization pass.
Automatic score direction includes four of the same author's music prompts from
DrawnExplainers/sets/not-arbitrary (Chinese characters, card suits, chess pieces,
and Roman numerals) as examples for the episode writer.

Android uses OkHttp (Square, Apache-2.0), Kotlin and kotlinx.coroutines
(JetBrains, Apache-2.0), and the standard Gradle wrapper (Apache-2.0).
Android prompt assets are generated from this repository's attributed prompts.
